DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The pptthhrreeaadd__cclleeaannuupp__ppoopp() function pops the top cleanup routine off of
     the current threads cleanup routine stack, and, if _e_x_e_c_u_t_e is non-zero,
     it will execute the function.  If there is no cleanup routine then
     pptthhrreeaadd__cclleeaannuupp__ppoopp() does nothing.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__cclleeaannuupp__ppoopp() function is implemented as a macro that closes
     a block.  Invocations of this function must appear as standalone state‐
     ments that are paired with an earlier call of pthread_cleanup_push(3) in
     the same lexical scope.

